      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since Precompile requires the full RenderPassDesc to be provided, it represents the outcome after applying the depth usage policy (added in follow-up CLs), so I think it mostly \"just works\".  The preferred serialized key system definitely just works.\n\nIn the future, if we pull back some of the explicitness of the RenderPassDesc, I think there are options that we can do to limit the precompile:\n1. For kAlways/kNever, we just generate the fixed depth/stencil settings required.\n2. For avoid internal-only, we sort of already track when we\u0027re in an image filter so that could activate the depth-less RP mode.  We\u0027d also then double up things for simple image draws that cover the other internal-use surfaces.\n3. For when-required, we\u0027d have to always double up the pipelines, but we may also limit when-required to cases where we have dynamic attachments or dynamic depth/stencil state, such that it wouldn\u0027t require duplicate pipelines.",
